RUN: %PLC -c --fpic %S/interface_constructors_lib.st -o %t.lib.o
RUN: %COMPILE -i %S/interface_constructors_lib.st %S/interface_constructors_main.st %t.lib.o && %RUN | %CHECK %s
RUN: %COMPILE --generate-external-constructors -i %S/interface_constructors_lib.st %S/interface_constructors_main.st %t.lib.o && %RUN | %CHECK %s
RUN: sed -E 's/^(TYPE|INTERFACE|FUNCTION_BLOCK|FUNCTION) /{external} \1 /' %S/interface_constructors_lib.st > %t.external.st
RUN: %COMPILE %t.external.st %S/interface_constructors_main.st %t.lib.o && %RUN | %CHECK %s

interface_constructors_lib.st declares interfaces whose methods and properties
use types with constructors: STRING[n], WSTRING[n], ARRAY, subrange, ARRAY OF
interface and POINTER TO parameters, inputs with default values, STRING[n] and
ARRAY return values, VAR_OUTPUT and VAR_IN_OUT strings, REFERENCE TO and REF_TO
parameters, STRING[n] and ARRAY properties with getters and setters, methods
of extended interfaces (also of an interface that extends two), a WSTRING[n]
input with a default value and a REFERENCE TO interface parameter.
IDeclaredOnly has no implementor and adds an inline enum parameter, inline
nested arrays, a REFERENCE TO return value, an ARRAY[*] OF STRING[n] parameter
and pointers to inline arrays.
It is compiled to its own object. The program includes it, links that object,
and calls through the interfaces into a library type and into a program type.
Only the object built from interface_constructors_lib.st may define the
constructors of these parameter types.

The last build compiles the declarations of interface_constructors_lib.st as
source, with each one marked {external}. It must give the same result as -i.

